# The scraper's frozen page snapshots are evidence, not source. Git normalising
# their line endings on checkout would change the bytes of a file whose whole
# purpose is to be the exact page a spec was verified against.
#
# Measured: extraction output is currently byte-identical under CRLF and LF across
# all 50 replayable sources, so this changes no test result today. It is here so
# that stays true if anything ever hashes these files -- cache.py already computes
# a content_sha1 over freshly fetched pages, and expected.json records a
# verified_content_sha1, so the machinery to make a checkout matter exists.
data/scraper/specs/**/snapshot.html -text
data/scraper/specs/**/page.pdf      -text binary
